WEBVTT

00:00:06.953 --> 00:00:08.259
Think, Neville.
Think!

00:00:08.303 --> 00:00:11.088
[ creaking]

00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:13.395
Riddikulus!

00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:17.834
[ Professor Lupin
and students laughing]

00:00:17.877 --> 00:00:19.836
Wonderful, Neville!
Wonderful!

00:00:19.879 --> 00:00:21.316
Incredible. Okay.

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:24.057
To the back, Neville.
Everyone, form a line!

00:00:24.841 --> 00:00:26.190
[ grunts]

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:27.365
Ow, stop!

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:29.976
[ indistinct voices]

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.022
LUPIN:
Form a line! I want everyone

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:35.025
to picture the thing
they fear the very most

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.854
and turn it into
something... funny.

00:00:37.897 --> 00:00:38.898
Next!

00:00:38.942 --> 00:00:40.378
Ron!

00:00:40.422 --> 00:00:43.381
[ swing music plays]

00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:44.339
Concentrate.

00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:45.557
Face your fear.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.820
Be brave!

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.911
[ whimpers]

00:00:56.786 --> 00:00:57.830
[ snapping]

00:00:57.874 --> 00:00:59.441
Come on, wand
at the ready, Ron.

00:00:59.484 --> 00:01:00.398
Wand at the ready.

00:01:00.442 --> 00:01:01.530
Riddikulus!

00:01:01.573 --> 00:01:03.445
[ laughing]

00:01:03.488 --> 00:01:04.576
Yes!

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.708
[ chuckling]:
You see?

00:01:05.751 --> 00:01:08.406
Very good!
Very good!

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:09.625
Marvelous!

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:10.713
Absolutely,

00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:12.236
very, very enjoyable.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.238
Parvati! Next!
Parvati.

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:15.370
[ laughing]

00:01:15.413 --> 00:01:17.241
Show us what
you see.

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:19.939
[ whooshing]

00:01:21.593 --> 00:01:25.206
[ hissing]

00:01:27.295 --> 00:01:31.037
Keep your nerve steady.

00:01:31.081 --> 00:01:32.996
Riddikulus!

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:34.171
[ laughs]

00:01:34.215 --> 00:01:34.954
And next!

00:01:34.998 --> 00:01:35.999
Step up! Step up!

00:01:36.042 --> 00:01:37.783
Wonderful, wonderful.

00:01:37.827 --> 00:01:39.307
Very good...

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.961
[ raucous swing music
continues]

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.450
[ low moaning]

00:01:52.929 --> 00:01:55.061
Here!

00:01:55.105 --> 00:01:58.587
[ moaning]

00:02:00.806 --> 00:02:01.764
Riddikulus!

00:02:01.807 --> 00:02:03.331
[ air whooshing]

00:02:03.374 --> 00:02:07.248
[ gasping]

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.121
[ thudding]

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.122
Right, well,
sorry about that.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.341
Uh, that's enough
for today.

00:02:13.384 --> 00:02:14.820
If you'd all like
to collect your books

00:02:14.864 --> 00:02:15.952
from the back
of the class,

00:02:15.995 --> 00:02:17.083
that's the end
of the lesson.

00:02:17.127 --> 00:02:18.389
Thank you.[ groaning]

00:02:18.433 --> 00:02:19.608
Sorry. Sorry.
Go on.

00:02:19.651 --> 00:02:21.392
You can have too much
of a good thing.

00:02:21.436 --> 00:02:23.307
[ swing music continues]

00:02:23.351 --> 00:02:25.266
PROFESSOR McGONAGALL:
Now, remember,

00:02:25.309 --> 00:02:28.181
these visits to Hogsmeade
Village are a privilege.

00:02:28.225 --> 00:02:32.229
Should your behavior reflect
poorly on the school in any way,

00:02:32.273 --> 00:02:34.797
that privilege shall
not be extended again.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.931
No permission form signed,
no visiting the village.

00:02:38.975 --> 00:02:40.281
That's the rule, Potter.

00:02:40.324 --> 00:02:42.152
All those with
permission, follow me.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.632
Those without, stay put.

00:02:43.675 --> 00:02:44.937
But Professor,
I thought

00:02:44.981 --> 00:02:46.330
if you signed it,
then I could go.

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:48.376
I can't. Only a parent
or a guardian can sign.

00:02:48.419 --> 00:02:52.293
Since I am neither,
it would be inappropriate.

00:02:54.425 --> 00:02:56.340
I'm sorry, Potter.

00:02:56.384 --> 00:02:59.822
That's my final word.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:04.217
Forget about it, guys.
See you later.

00:03:13.314 --> 00:03:15.751
♪

00:03:17.318 --> 00:03:18.493
HARRY:
Professor,

00:03:18.536 --> 00:03:19.842
can I ask you something?

00:03:19.885 --> 00:03:21.365
LUPIN:
You want to know

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:23.193
why I stopped you
facing that boggart, yes?

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.977
I would have thought
it'd be obvious.

00:03:25.021 --> 00:03:28.067
I assumed it would take
the shape of Lord Voldemort.

00:03:28.111 --> 00:03:31.680
I did think of Voldemort...
at first.

00:03:31.723 --> 00:03:34.987
But then I remembered
that night on the train...

00:03:35.031 --> 00:03:36.337
and the dementor.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.903
Well, I'm very impressed.

00:03:37.947 --> 00:03:41.037
That suggests that what you fear
the most is fear itself.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.169
This is very wise.

00:03:43.213 --> 00:03:44.693
Before I fainted...

00:03:44.736 --> 00:03:46.869
I heard something.

00:03:46.912 --> 00:03:49.393
A woman...

00:03:49.437 --> 00:03:50.699
screaming.

00:03:50.742 --> 00:03:52.396
Well, dementors force us

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.312
to relive
our very worst memories.

00:03:55.356 --> 00:03:57.532
Our pain becomes
their power.

00:03:57.575 --> 00:03:59.708
I think it was
my mother...

00:03:59.751 --> 00:04:02.885
the night she
was murdered.

00:04:03.712 --> 00:04:06.410
You know, the very first time
I saw you, Harry,

00:04:06.454 --> 00:04:09.065
I recognized you
immediately.

00:04:09.108 --> 00:04:12.416
Not by your scar;
by your eyes.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.680
They're your mother Lily's.

00:04:15.724 --> 00:04:18.422
Yes. Oh, yes.

00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:21.207
I knew her.

00:04:22.513 --> 00:04:26.474
Your mother was there for me
at a time when no one else was.

00:04:26.517 --> 00:04:29.781
Not only was she a
singularly gifted witch,

00:04:29.825 --> 00:04:33.437
she was also
an uncommonly kind woman.

00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:36.875
She had a way of seeing
the beauty in others.

00:04:36.919 --> 00:04:39.312
Even, and perhaps
most especially,

00:04:39.356 --> 00:04:44.230
when that person could not
see it in themselves.

00:04:44.579 --> 00:04:48.800
Well, your father, James,
on the other hand, he, uh...

00:04:48.844 --> 00:04:51.020
[ chuckles]:
he had a certain,

00:04:51.063 --> 00:04:54.327
shall we say,
talent for trouble.

00:04:55.154 --> 00:05:01.422
A talent, rumor has it...
he passed on to you.

00:05:04.599 --> 00:05:08.298
You're more like them
than you know, Harry.

00:05:08.777 --> 00:05:13.172
In time, you'll come to see
just how much.

00:05:15.218 --> 00:05:16.785
RON:
Honeyduke's Sweet Shop

00:05:16.828 --> 00:05:18.134
is brilliant.

00:05:18.177 --> 00:05:19.875
But nothing beats
Zonko's Joke Shop.

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:22.181
We never did get a chance to go
to The Shrieking Shack, though.

00:05:22.225 --> 00:05:23.444
You heard that it's the most...

00:05:23.487 --> 00:05:25.054
HARRY:
The most haunted building

00:05:25.097 --> 00:05:27.926
in Britain, yeah, I heard.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.014
What's going on?

00:05:29.058 --> 00:05:30.233
Huh, probably
Neville's

00:05:30.276 --> 00:05:31.539
forgotten the
password again.

00:05:31.582 --> 00:05:33.802
Hey!Oh! You're there.

00:05:33.845 --> 00:05:36.500
PERCY:
Uh, let me through, please.

00:05:36.544 --> 00:05:38.676
Excuse me!
I'm Head Boy!

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.983
[ indistinct voices]

00:05:41.026 --> 00:05:42.245
Get back... all of you.

00:05:42.288 --> 00:05:43.551
No one is to enter
this dormitory

00:05:43.594 --> 00:05:45.509
until it has been
fully searched.

00:05:45.553 --> 00:05:46.467
[ gasping]

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.685
The Fat Lady! She's gone!

00:05:47.729 --> 00:05:49.600
KNIGHT IN PAINTING:
Who goes there?

00:05:49.644 --> 00:05:50.558
RON:
Serves her right.

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:51.602
She was
a terrible singer.

00:05:51.646 --> 00:05:52.864
HERMIONE:
It's not funny, Ron.

00:05:52.908 --> 00:05:53.865
[ baby crying]

00:05:53.909 --> 00:05:54.997
[ woman laughs]

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.999
PERCY:
Keep calm, everyone.

00:05:57.042 --> 00:05:59.828
Ravenclaws,
back to your common room.

00:05:59.871 --> 00:06:01.960
[ woman trilling]

00:06:02.004 --> 00:06:03.005
[ groaning]

00:06:03.048 --> 00:06:04.528
[ crying]

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:06.617
PERCY:
All right, be quiet.

00:06:06.661 --> 00:06:08.140
FILCH:
Make way!

00:06:08.184 --> 00:06:09.141
The Headmaster's here!

00:06:09.185 --> 00:06:10.186
Come on.
Move! Move!

00:06:10.229 --> 00:06:12.710
You heard!
Move!

